UID:gasworks-residency-east-africa-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T115020Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gasworks Residency 2027: Artists Based in East Africa
DESCRIPTION:Gasworks residency open call for an early-career contemporary v
 isual artist based in East Africa. The eleven-week\, fully funded residenc
 y runs at Gasworks in London from 7 April to 22 June 2027. Gasworks' resid
 ency programme supports professional development\, cultural exchange and a
 rtistic experimentation\, hosting up to twenty residencies a year\; reside
 ncies are self-led\, non-prescriptive and process-based\, with artists exp
 ected to lead on the research and production of their own work while Gaswo
 rks provides administrative\, pastoral and curatorial support during offic
 e hours. The residency includes studio visits with Gasworks staff\, extern
 al curators\, artists and educational groups\, at least two individual stu
 dio visits with other artists\, curators and arts professionals\, networki
 ng opportunities\, a dedicated residency page on the Gasworks website with
  a short video interview filmed and edited by Gasworks\, and an Open Studi
 o event and presentation of the work and research developed during the res
 idency on 12 June 2027. ELIGIBILITY: early-career contemporary visual arti
 sts based in Burundi\, the Chagos Archipelago\, Comoros\, Djibouti\, Ethio
 pia\, Eritrea\, the French Southern Territories\, Kenya\, Madagascar\, Mal
 awi\, Mauritius\, Mayotte\, Mozambique\, Reunion\, Rwanda\, Seychelles\, S
 omalia\, South Sudan\, Uganda\, the United Republic of Tanzania or Zambia 
 only. Applicants should have at least a moderate level of spoken English a
 nd feel comfortable discussing their work in English. The residency is off
 ered subject to approval of the visa application. Deadline 28 September 20
 26\, 12:00 UTC. No fee.\n\nOrganisation: Gasworks\nLocation: Gasworks\, Lo
 ndon\, United Kingdom. Applicants must be based in East Africa: Burundi\, 
 Chagos Archipelago\, Comoros\, Djibouti\, Ethiopia\, Eritrea\, French Sout
 hern Territories\, Kenya\, Madagascar\, Malawi\, Mauritius\, Mayotte\, Moz
 ambique\, Reunion\, Rwanda\, Seychelles\, Somalia\, South Sudan\, Uganda\,
  United Republic of Tanzania or Zambia.\nAward: Fully funded eleven-week r
 esidency: 24/7 access to a fully accessible private studio at Gasworks\; s
 ingle-room accommodation in Gasworks' Residency House (shared two-storey h
 ouse with three communal bathrooms and a kitchen)\; economy return flights
  and taxi transfers from the artist's home country to London (one cabin an
 d one hold bag)\; all visa costs and visa-application support\; weekly sti
 pend of GBP 175 for living expenses\; materials budget of up to GBP 800\; 
 prepaid TFL Zones 1+2 travel card for unlimited central London travel thro
 ughout the residency\; access to Gasworks' basic tools and AV equipment su
 bject to availability. No application fee.\nDuration: Eleven weeks\, 7 Apr
 il to 22 June 2027\n\nMore: https://www.gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/resi
 dency-open-call-for-artists-based-in-east-africa-2027?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/residency-open-call-for-artis
 ts-based-in-east-africa-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Gasworks\, London\, United Kingdom. Applicants must be based in Ea
 st Africa: Burundi\, Chagos Archipelago\, Comoros\, Djibouti\, Ethiopia\, 
 Eritrea\, French Southern Territories\, Kenya\, Madagascar\, Malawi\, Maur
 itius\, Mayotte\, Mozambique\, Reunion\, Rwanda\, Seychelles\, Somalia\, S
 outh Sudan\, Uganda\, United Republic of Tanzania or Zambia.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bold-lab-bold-fellow-oxford-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T115020Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: BOLD Fellow\, British Open-ended Learning and Discovery L
 ab
DESCRIPTION:The British Open-ended Learning and Discovery (BOLD) Lab is a n
 ew UKRI-funded initiative establishing an AI research laboratory led from 
 the University of Oxford\, bringing more than 80 researchers from Oxford\,
  UCL and Imperial College London under one vision. It carries an initial i
 nvestment of around GBP 8 million with the potential for a further GBP 22 
 million extending the investment over six years\, making it one of the UK'
 s largest bets on fundamental AI research. The lab's remit is ambitious\, 
 high-risk work on the fundamental science of artificial intelligence\, alo
 ngside training future leaders in the field. THE ROLE: up to 12 BOLD Fello
 ws are being recruited across the three universities. Fellows are expected
  to operate with a high level of independence and responsibility\, setting
  their own research direction\, publishing at the highest level\, and ment
 oring junior researchers and doctoral students. They also play a leading r
 ole in managing the lab and take responsibility for developing its strateg
 ic and scientific direction\, with primary responsibility for a programme 
 of independent funded research projects. The posting frames the draw as ex
 ceptional independence\, direct collaboration with world-leading colleague
 s across the three institutions\, access to substantial and rapidly growin
 g compute\, and real influence over the intellectual direction and culture
  of a major national lab. WHO SHOULD APPLY: senior researchers with an est
 ablished\, original research track record in AI or a closely related field
 \, who are a recognised authority in their area. HOW TO APPLY: submit an o
 nline application with a covering letter or supporting statement\, a CV\, 
 and details of two referees. Informal enquiries are welcomed beforehand to
  the BOLD Exec Team at boldexec-team@eng.ox.ac.uk. NOTE: this is a salarie
